M61 — CI TS/CDK dependency guard, 2026-09-06 local macOS / Python 3.13
Scope: .github/workflows/gate.yml, tests/_ts_toolchain.py (new),
tests/test_registry_preview_ui.py, tests/test_registry_planner_stack.py,
tests/test_ci_ts_dependency_guard.py (new). The commit also updates six
status/plan/lesson documents and this evidence file (12 files total).

Problem measured: gate.yml never set up Node/npm for dashboard/ or
src/stacks/, so tests/test_registry_preview_ui.py and
tests/test_registry_planner_stack.py each `pytest.skip` when
node_modules/.bin/tsc is absent. On a runner without that toolchain both
files would skip on every run and the TS request/Invoke contract and the
planner CDK synthesis would never actually be checked in CI, while
`gh pr checks` shows the same green as a real pass (Risk 12(2)).

Fix, in two independent halves:
1. gate.yml: actions/setup-node@v4 (node 22, cache: npm,
   cache-dependency-path = dashboard/package-lock.json +
   src/stacks/package-lock.json) followed by `npm ci` in each of
   dashboard/ and src/stacks/, before `make check` runs. Mirrors the
   existing terraform-init step's reasoning (comment left in gate.yml).
2. tests/_ts_toolchain.py: require_ts_toolchain(compiler, node_available,
   hint) — returns silently if present; otherwise pytest.skip() unless
   CI or GITHUB_ACTIONS is set in the environment, in which case
   pytest.fail(). Both contract test files now call this instead of a
   bare `if not compiler.exists(): pytest.skip(...)`.

Regression coverage (tests/test_ci_ts_dependency_guard.py, 7 new tests):
- present toolchain -> no skip, no fail
- missing toolchain, CI/GITHUB_ACTIONS unset -> pytest.skip.Exception
- missing toolchain, CI=true -> pytest.fail.Exception
- missing toolchain, GITHUB_ACTIONS=true -> pytest.fail.Exception
- compiler present but node missing, CI=true -> pytest.fail.Exception
- both contract files are grepped for the literal call
  `require_ts_toolchain(` so a future revert to a bare `pytest.skip` is
  intended to cause a gate failure. M62 later reproduced a false green
  when the call text remained only in a comment; see the follow-up log.

Local verification actually performed (no network fetch, no npm
install/ci run, no remote CI, no push, no deploy):
- dashboard/node_modules and src/stacks/node_modules were already present
  in this worktree from prior local work, so the TS contract and CDK
  synthesis tests ran for real (not skipped) both before and after this
  change: `tsc` compiled, `node` executed the contract script /
  Template.fromStack() synthesis, and every assertion in both files
  passed.
- `make check` before this change: 2679 passed, 2 skipped
  (docs/STATUS.md baseline, same machine).
- `make check` after this change: 2686 passed, 2 skipped, 2688
  collected (+7, exactly the new guard-behaviour tests; the two
  contract files' own test counts are unchanged because their fixtures
  still resolve the same local toolchain).
- Did not run `npm ci`/`npm install` here — the toolchain used was
  whatever this worktree already had installed. Whether `npm ci` itself
  succeeds against the committed lockfiles on a fresh ubuntu-latest
  runner is therefore unverified by this session; that is the
  "npm 다운로드·원격 CI 실행" the task explicitly excluded from this
  iteration's scope.

